  "albumInformation": "<p>\"The Ghost of Reality\" contains two new compositions    made by Al Margolis in 2007. In \"Too Too\", he employs buzzing drones    and hat sounds like someone fidgeting a loose cable or a microphone, accompanied    by whining tones to create a subtle atmosphere of uneasy sillyness. The second    track, \"Imp\", finds Margolis toying around with his ARP 2600 synth,    generating a seemingly random sequence of clicks, squeaks and filtered noise    that eventually constitute a complex rhythmical texture.</p>",
